## Regression test: -rewrite must not crash on non-PIE dynamic binaries and
## must patch absolute data pointers that have no dynamic relocations.
##
## Two bugs are covered:
##  1. patchELFSymTabs aborted with "Cannot locate fragment containing
##     secondary entrypoint" for STT_FUNC symbols pointing inside a PLT
##     (non-PIE links resolve undefined-function symbols to their PLT
##     stub): PLT functions are emitted without a CFG, so address
##     translation returned 0. The address now maps linearly inside the
##     PLT section.
##  2. Non-PIE binaries store link-time-resolved absolute pointers (e.g.
##     in .init_array) with no dynamic relocations; when -rewrite moves
##     the sections the stale absolute values must be patched in the
##     output from the -q .rela.* records.
##
## The test asserts that llvm-bolt completes and that the .init_array
## pointer in the output references the new .text address of the function.

# REQUIRES: system-linux

# RUN: %clang %cflags -shared -fPIC %S/Inputs/rewrite-nopie-stub.c -o %t.so
# RUN: %clang %cflags -O0 -Wl,-q -no-pie -fuse-ld=lld %S/Inputs/rewrite-nopie-initarray.c %t.so -o %t.orig -Wl,-e,_start
# RUN: llvm-bolt %t.orig -o %t.bolt -rewrite
# RUN: TEXT=`llvm-readelf -SW %t.bolt | awk '$3==".text" {print $5}'` && INIT=`llvm-readelf -x .init_array %t.bolt | awk '/0x0/ {w=$2; print "0x" substr(w,7,2) substr(w,5,2) substr(w,3,2) substr(w,1,2)}'` && python3 -c "import sys; t=int('$TEXT',16); v=int('$INIT',16); sys.exit(0 if t <= v < t + 0x10000 else 1)" && echo init-patched
